00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:10.583
She says she doesn't want them

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:11.450
to make her kids

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.351
don't go to public school.

00:09:12.351 --> 00:09:13.319
No, they have never been.

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:13.686
She hopes

00:09:13.686 --> 00:09:14.954
maybe by high school

00:09:14.954 --> 00:09:16.088
the schools will be

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:17.957
good enough for her kids.

00:09:17.957 --> 00:09:18.658
The other liberals

00:09:18.658 --> 00:09:19.892
we talked to the liberal parents

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.093
whose kids do go to that school.

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:22.895
They say it's not the majority opinion.

00:09:22.895 --> 00:09:24.897
So, for example, one parent

00:09:24.897 --> 00:09:26.966
complained about five books

00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:28.768
and that meant that the district

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:29.835
had to create committees

00:09:29.835 --> 00:09:31.304
to determine

00:09:31.304 --> 00:09:32.838
whether those books were obscene

00:09:32.838 --> 00:09:33.673
or they could stay.

00:09:33.673 --> 00:09:35.341
And in the end, all five stayed.

00:09:35.341 --> 00:09:36.976
But one parent who served on that

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:37.643
committee said

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:39.211
it was just a huge waste of time

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.980
and resources.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:41.781
Ellery, thank you

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:42.748
really fascinating report.

